  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000) dominates over image (ResNet50) by a wide margin (0.591 vs 0.208), and the multimodal gain over RNA-only is modest (~0.028). The best RNA-only config (config_002: multi-profile, avgpool) achieves 0.591, but we have no evidence yet about whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can capture nonlinear structure that PCA misses. Question: Does scvi_n200 improve over PCA n2000 in the same RNA-only, multi-profile, avgpool setting? This is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002, isolating the RNA encoder effect without confounding from image or fusion choices. Why this is the best next experiment: RNA is the dominant signal source, so understanding whether a learned encoder can push RNA-only performance above 0.591 is the highest-leverage question. If scvi helps here, it will likely compound in the multimodal setting; if it does not, we can rule out RNA encoder complexity as a bottleneck and focus budget on image or fusion improvements. This avoids the risk of changing the RNA encoder in the already-complex multimodal setting where a small effect could be masked by other factors."
}

